BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260918
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260919
SUMMARY:Millennium Actress (2001)
DESCRIPTION:Genre: Animation\, Drama\, Romance\\nRating: 7.848/10\\n\\nAn actress's life told through the films she made — Satoshi Kon dissolves the boundary between biography and cinema itself. Time and fiction collapse beautifully.
UID:bbd402d80eee983e3420a7157c0c66c1@jellyfin-films
DTSTAMP:20260823T074754Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260919
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260920
SUMMARY:Stone Skipping (2020)
DESCRIPTION:Genre: Drama\\nRating: 6.7/10\\n\\nKim Dae-myung's committed physical performance carries a rural drama exploring prejudice and ableism with a patient\, contemplative pace. The film asks difficult questions about community trust and the fragility of innocence.
UID:dae65950a6d092d9d7ede43795e29609@jellyfin-films
DTSTAMP:20260823T074754Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260920
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260921
SUMMARY:Blue Is the Warmest Colour (2013)
DESCRIPTION:Genre: Drama\, Romance\\nRating: 7.071/10\\n\\nKechiche films a relationship from first glance to last argument. The close-ups of faces eating\, talking\, crying are unflinching — the intimacy is in the duration.
UID:ad8ac7dd7d65ab4af5409a1f926ae065@jellyfin-films
DTSTAMP:20260823T074754Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260921
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260922
SUMMARY:I Saw the Devil (2010)
DESCRIPTION:Genre: Horror\, Thriller\\nRating: 7.8/10\\n\\nA secret agent hunts the man who murdered his fiancée — but keeps letting him go. Kim Jee-woon directs revenge as a game that consumes the player. Relentless.
UID:613c7e92bf35841afac5dae6fe1e251b@jellyfin-films
DTSTAMP:20260823T074754Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260922
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260923
SUMMARY:Journals of Musan (2010)
DESCRIPTION:Genre: Drama\\nRating: 6.7/10\\n\\nA North Korean defector in Seoul\, invisible to everyone around him. Shot with documentary-level austerity — Park Jung-bum's performance is so lived-in it barely feels like acting.
UID:6bd61edd21c8da4990b14c6bdb73a5f5@jellyfin-films
DTSTAMP:20260823T074754Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260923
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260924
SUMMARY:Begin Again (2014)
DESCRIPTION:Genre: Comedy\, Drama\, Music\, Romance\\nRating: 7.233/10\\n\\nA disgraced producer and a heartbroken songwriter record an album across New York City. The split-headphone scene is pure cinema — two people hearing the same city differently.
UID:b45879ffa87dbcecfc3f4aa0ed3c64be@jellyfin-films
DTSTAMP:20260823T074754Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260924
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260925
SUMMARY:The God of Cookery (1996)
DESCRIPTION:Genre: Comedy\, Drama\, Fantasy\\nRating: 7.2/10\\n\\nStephen Chow as a fraudulent celebrity chef who must learn to actually cook. Hong Kong comedy operating at peak absurdity — the food competitions are staged like kung fu battles.
UID:179a4b02414ead9321197762ab44155c@jellyfin-films
DTSTAMP:20260823T074754Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260926
SUMMARY:The Road Home (1999)
DESCRIPTION:Genre: Drama\, Romance\\nRating: 7.5/10\\n\\nZhang Yimou's simplest film — a young woman runs to meet a man. The past is in color\, the present in black and white. Zhang Ziyi before stardom\, luminous and grounded.
UID:39845511860efaed8680069e283f765b@jellyfin-films
DTSTAMP:20260823T074754Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260926
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260927
SUMMARY:The Martian (2015)
DESCRIPTION:Genre: Adventure\, Drama\, Science Fiction\\nRating: 7.7/10\\n\\nRidley Scott directs the most optimistic survival film ever — Matt Damon sciences his way off Mars. The problem-solving IS the entertainment.
UID:b7c705c83864ef41954972727876cdc9@jellyfin-films
DTSTAMP:20260823T074754Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260927
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:Pawn (2020)
DESCRIPTION:Genre: Comedy\, Drama\, Family\\nRating: 8.329/10\\n\\nA loan shark takes a baby as collateral and ends up raising her. The premise sounds absurd\; the film earns its sincerity by committing to every emotional beat.
UID:a33ef29fbcef89f14bb6f81314277d20@jellyfin-films
DTSTAMP:20260823T074754Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260928
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260929
SUMMARY:Walk the Line (2005)
DESCRIPTION:Genre: Drama\, Music\, Romance\\nRating: 7.498/10\\n\\nJoaquin Phoenix and Reese Witherspoon performed their own vocals. The discipline of that choice — learning Cash and Carter's instruments\, voices\, and postures — is the film's integrity.
UID:0e550f1585910630e6b9245028f220fc@jellyfin-films
DTSTAMP:20260823T074754Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260929
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260930
SUMMARY:Into the Wild (2007)
DESCRIPTION:Genre: Adventure\, Drama\\nRating: 7.796/10\\n\\nSean Penn follows a young man into the Alaskan wilderness. The landscape cinematography by Éric Gautier is seductive by design — the beauty is the danger.
UID:b855b4c3bb36abfe8bc57394798c04c2@jellyfin-films
DTSTAMP:20260823T074754Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Extreme Job (2019)
DESCRIPTION:Genre: Action\, Comedy\, Crime\\nRating: 7.193/10\\n\\nNarcotics cops go undercover running a fried chicken restaurant and it becomes wildly successful. The funniest Korean film in years — the comedy is in the competence.
UID:e8f68c0f9419a8bf96726c534c97c8f2@jellyfin-films
DTSTAMP:20260823T074754Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
